  "term": "sensorimotor rhythm",
  "definition": "Sensorimotor rhythm is an EEG frequency band around 12–15 Hz linked to motor-related brain activity. In this packet, stronger or more stable SMR synchronization is described as supporting efficient movement preparation and consistent motor execution, especially under pressure.",
